`allow.hosts` contains `example.com.`. A trailing dot names the DNS root explicitly; `example.com.` and `example.com` would be two spellings of one host, and the contract admits one. SPEC §4.4: a host is a lower-case DNS name, an IPv4 literal or `localhost`, with an optional single leading `*.` label, or the bare `*`; two implementations must not disagree about what a host entry names.
